  "acpAgents": {
    "hermes": {
      "command": "hermes",
      "args": ["acp"],
      "env": {
        "PATH": "$HOME/.local/bin:$HOME/.hermes/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"
      },
      "wrapperModel": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
      "timeoutMs": 300000,
      "permissionMode": "allow",
      "description": "Hermes Agent — messaging (Signal), web search, browser automation, cron scheduling, voice mode, home automation. Persistent autonomous agent that learns across sessions.",
      "orchestratorPrompt": "@hermes (via ACP)\n- External agent: Hermes Agent with 70+ tools, Signal gateway, cron scheduler, browser automation, voice mode.\n- **Delegate when:** Sending Signal messages or notifications · Web scraping / browser automation · Managing cron / scheduled tasks · Voice interaction · Home Assistant / home automation · Any life-automation or non-coding task where Hermes' platform gateways are the right tool.\n- **Don't delegate:** Coding tasks, code review, file operations, architecture decisions — these are OpenCode's domain.\n- Delegation wraps Hermes as a sandboxed ACP subagent with read-only access to the conversation prompt."
    }
  }
